{"id": "EUVD-2026-103868", "enisaUuid": "f7eb19c6-0dba-3fb1-9288-f469f36ce76d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/mediatek: Add missing IS_ERR check for ovl_adaptor platform device\n\nplatform_device_register_data() can fail and return an ERR_PTR, but the\nreturn value is used without checking, leading to an invalid pointer\nbeing stored in ddp_comp[].dev and passed to component_match_add() and\nmtk_ddp_comp_init(), which could result in a kernel crash.\n\nAdd an IS_ERR() check to jump to the error handling path on failure.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0ffb09cf1bf2a0f301f51fb45371c09dc78fcd0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4acac370aad2d4895a82f40b2f03e9ef70eecaa6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88f8a92dcb0cb154774595dee7226458de4cbd38", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aeef8a8537bcfb26689edb36ed905b8b2873001c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bce7698e2e6565bb765bd0522337f29f5f312624"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98783", "GHSA-gxv2-4p27-m9pp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "051699c4-152c-3601-bb87-f105667c21ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0da8a1b1-92de-3434-9b56-a670e9e46109", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "2e2908f9-4c54-346b-861c-c290364d252a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0d9eee9118b77e51eeafc5bf4d008fac97035d56 <bce7698e2e6565bb765bd0522337f29f5f312624"}, {"id": "4f5f0ee9-94ca-35ba-8506-db73ed366621", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "504ce0fd-4e7e-340b-9352-773b626f1d50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "62a7390b-ef11-3276-b